#
# charon: only strict start-from selections must declare an item
#
# 153a39d made every start-from selection that declares no item an error. That also fired for
# `--start-from-if-exists` patterns that resolve to nothing, and for the implicit default `crate`
# selection of a crate that defines no item. Record whether each selection is strict: explicit
# `--start-from` patterns, `--start-from-attribute` and `--start-from-pub` are; if-exists patterns
# and the implicit `crate` are not. Report the error without a misleading dummy span.
#
# start_from.out now declares the items the std-path patterns select (`std::iter::once`,
# `std::clone::Clone::clone_from`, `std::slice::Iter::as_slice`, `u32::wrapping_add`) and their
# dependencies: re-matching the patterns against the items' Charon names (`core::...`) never
# declared them, so these selections silently yielded nothing.

